<title>BULGARIA: Bulgaria offers 10 bln levs 1-yr T-bills Thursday.</title>
<headline>Bulgaria offers 10 bln levs 1-yr T-bills Thursday.</headline>
<dateline>SOFIA 1997-06-26</dateline>
<text>
<p>Bulgaria's Finance Ministry will offer on Thursday 10 billion levs of 12-month floating interest T-bills with no minimum acceptable price set in advance, the central bank said in a statement.</p>
<p>Interest on the issue is due at maturity. It is set equal to the central bank main interest rate and is adjusted each time the rate changes.</p>
<p>The main rate is now set at an effecive annual 16.30 percent calculated through the accumulation of monthly accruals.</p>
<p>Details of the offer follow:</p>
<p> Issue number	   BG3040697024</p>
<p> Maturity		 12 months</p>
<p> Par value		10 bln levs</p>
<p> Auction date	   June 26</p>
<p> Issue date	     June 26</p>
<p> Maturity date	  June 25, 1998</p>
<p>-- Sofia Newsroom, (++359-2) 91188</p>
